# MAESTRO example: LTU Festo MPS line
#
# Umbrella of this use case: the ontology header, which imports the module files under core/ and ext/.
# Single-file form: line-merged.ttl (written by tools/merge_usecases.py).
#
# Notes carried over from the former plant.ttl, product.ttl, which this use case was split from;
# section titles and file names in them refer to those files.
#
# [plant.ttl]
# LTU FESTO MPS LINE - PLANT (DESIGN TIME)
#
# The MPS line as a production unit: the AutomationML links between
# neighbouring stations, i.e. the material hand-over ports and the
# optical StationLink pairs. The line itself (ltu:MPSLine, an
# maestro:WorkCenter) is in shared/shared.ttl. Imports the four station
# plants.
#
# The line order (1 Distributing, 2 Testing, 3 Processing, 4 Handling)
# follows the Festo station numbering and the combination matrices of
# the manuals; the LTU layout itself is not stated in the documents.
#
# LINE TOPOLOGY (AutomationML internal links)
#
# Material: each station's output port to the next station's input port.
# StationLink: the downstream station's transmitter (incoming side) faces
# the upstream station's receiver (outgoing side). Assumed line order.
#
# [product.ttl]
# LTU FESTO MPS LINE - PRODUCT (WORKPIECE AND LINE RECIPE)
#
# The workpiece the four stations handle and the line recipe that
# chains the four station cycles. Imports the line plant and the four
# station product files, so loading this file loads the whole line.
#
# WORKPIECE
#
# Processing assembly instructions: 'the basic body of an assemblable
# pneumatic cylinder'. Colours from the Testing and Handling manuals;
# heights from the Testing manual. Diameter, mass and the materials of
# the red and black workpieces are not stated, and no workpiece order
# number is given (so the product types carry no maestro:Identifier).
#
# LINE RECIPE
#
# One step per station, realised by the station's cycle skill; the
# station GRAFCETs are the control sequences inside each step.

@prefix rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#> .
@prefix owl: <http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#> .

<https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/line> a owl:Ontology ;
    rdfs:label "MAESTRO example: LTU Festo MPS line"@en ;
    rdfs:comment "Material and StationLink links between the four stations of the LTU Festo MPS line; workpiece type and variants and the line recipe Distributing -> Testing -> Processing -> Handling."@en ;
    owl:imports <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/distributing>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/handling>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/line/core/product>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/line/core/recipe>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/line/ext/automationml>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/processing>,
        <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/testing> ;
    owl:versionIRI <https://w3id.org/maestro/examples/ltu-festo-mps/line/0.1.0> ;
    owl:versionInfo "0.1.0" .
